Title: Night Shift

INT. WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain hammers the tin roof. REED (40s), a tall stranger with a shaved head and a scar across his chin, stacks CRATES. He wears a stained leather apron.

MARA (30s), wiry and quick, slips in through the side door holding a FLASHLIGHT.

MARA
You're late, Reed.

REED
Traffic.

EXT. ALLEY - NIGHT

MARA sprints between the bins. The tall stranger lumbers after her, breathing hard.

MARA
(into her phone)
Reed's on me. He's huge, and he's got that scar.

REED
Mara! Wait!

INT. WAREHOUSE - LATER

REED, soaked, sits on a crate under a bare bulb. MARA hands him the FLASHLIGHT.

MARA
You look like you lost a fight with the weather.
